[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large},scale=0.55]
\usetikzlibrary{angles,quotes}
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (6.128,5.142);
\coordinate (C) at (9.22,0);
\draw (A)--(B) node[midway,above left] {$8$};
\draw (B)--(C) node[midway,above right] {$6$};
\draw (A)--(C);
\pic[draw,"$40^{\circ}$",angle radius=1cm,angle eccentricity=1.4] {angle=C--A--B};
\pic[draw,"$\theta$",angle radius=1cm,angle eccentricity=1.5] {angle=B--C--A};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
There are two triangles fitting this data.
Find both possible values of $\theta$, correct to the nearest degree.

